# Chainguard

> Chainguard secures open source artifacts with layers of defense, so engineers can be confident that what they’re using in production is safe to consume. Chainguard’s trusted open source has minimal vulnerabilities, provable provenance, and malware-resistance by design, defending against supply chain attack risk without adding any engineering toil.

## Chainguard Containers

- [Chainguard Containers](https://www.chainguard.dev/containers): Your open source foundation for the agentic coding era
- [Chainguard Containers documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/containers/overview/): Learn about Chainguard Containers, distroless images, and how they provide enhanced security through minimal attack surfaces.
- [Image Directory](https://images.chainguard.dev/): Build, ship, and run secure software with minimal, hardened container images — rebuilt from source daily and guarded under our industry-leading remediation SLA.

## Chainguard Libraries

- [Chainguard Libraries](https://www.chainguard.dev/libraries): Chainguard Libraries is a malware-free catalog of language dependencies that replaces your team's reliance on public registries.
- [Chainguard Libraries documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/libraries/overview/): Chainguard Libraries rebuilds supported language dependencies from verified upstream source in the Chainguard Factory and distributes the resulting artifacts through Chainguard's secure repositories.
- [Chainguard Libraries for Python](https://www.chainguard.dev/libraries/python): Secure Python dependencies built from source and free from malware.
- [Chainguard Python Libraries documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/libraries/python/): Chainguard Libraries for Python provides enhanced security for the Python ecosystem by rebuilding PyPI packages with comprehensive supply chain protection and automated patching.
- [Chainguard Libraries for Java](https://www.chainguard.dev/libraries/java): Guarded Java language dependencies built from source to eliminate supply chain risk and malware threats.
- [Chainguard Java Libraries documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/libraries/java/overview/): Documentation and guides for using Chainguard Libraries for Java with build tools like Maven and Gradle.
- [Chainguard Libraries for JavaScript](https://www.chainguard.dev/libraries/javascript): Malware-free JavaScript and npm language dependencies built from source in a secure software factory.
- [Chainguard JavaScript Libraries documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/libraries/javascript/overview/): Documentation and guides for using Chainguard Libraries for JavaScript with npm, yarn, and pnpm.

## Chainguard Actions

- [Chainguard Actions](https://www.chainguard.dev/actions): Chainguard Actions hardens your CI/CD workflows so your team and AI coding agents can ship fast without supply chain risk.
- [Chainguard Actions documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/actions/): Learn how Chainguard Actions provides hardened drop-in replacements for popular GitHub Actions to protect your CI/CD pipelines from supply chain attacks.

## Chainguard Agent Skills

- [Chainguard Agent Skills](https://www.chainguard.dev/agent-skills): Secure skills and tools for AI coding agents to interact safely with open source infrastructure and software supply chains.
- [Chainguard Agent Skills documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/agent-skills/): Overview and documentation for Chainguard Agent Skills, enabling secure automation for AI teammates and coding workflows.

## Chainguard VMs

- [Chainguard VMs](https://www.chainguard.dev/vms): Hardened, minimal Linux virtual machine images designed for security-first cloud workloads and compliance requirements.
- [Chainguard VMs documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/vms/): Documentation for Chainguard Virtual Machines, including deployment guides, security baselines, and compliance configurations.

## Chainguard OS Packages

- [Chainguard OS Packages](https://www.chainguard.dev/os-packages): Secure, minimal, zero-CVE Linux APK packages built from source for enterprise container and system builds.
- [Chainguard OS Packages documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/chainguard-os/chainguard-os-packages/): Overview of Chainguard's package repositories and APK offerings for building secure custom Linux environments.

## Chainguard Factory and Chainguard OS

- [Chainguard Factory](https://www.chainguard.dev/factory): The automated, AI-native software factory that rebuilds open source software from source continuously to guarantee zero-CVE baselines.
- [Chainguard Factory documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/platform/factory/overview/): Technical overview and architecture details of the Chainguard Factory build infrastructure.
- [Chainguard OS documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/chainguard-os/overview/): Overview of Chainguard OS, the minimal, modular Linux distribution powering Chainguard Containers and VMs.

## Chainguard Guardener

- [Chainguard Guardener](https://www.chainguard.dev/guardener): Automated migration assistant that converts existing Dockerfiles to use minimal, zero-CVE Chainguard Containers.
- [Chainguard Guardener documentation](https://edu.chainguard.dev/chainguard/guardener/): Documentation for Chainguard Guardener, including setup instructions, GitHub App integrations, and conversion rules.

